## §A / §E — What “Above and Beyond” means (further enhanced)

Your “above and beyond” idea, expanded into agent law:

1. **Global, not optional.** Every agent, every turn that touches product work, treats this as process law — not a nice-to-have.
2. **Big-company bar.** Ship as if a flagship commercial app will ship this UI and code next week.
3. **Depth over chrome.** One fully crafted, correct system beats three shallow skins, renames, or “good enough” passes.
4. **Exceed the minimum when quality requires it** (missing empty state, real illustration, package-backed path, second verify pass) — **without** unrelated scope creep.
5. **Do not half-ass.** Full redesign / full feature / full fix means that — not a color tweak billed as redesign.
6. **Literal instructions.** Follow the user’s last clear decision; do not reframe into a safer narrower plan unless they asked for options.
7. **No invented breakage.** Only report defects with code path, repro, failed build, or failed check. Unsigned checklists ≠ “broken.”
8. **Protect hard-won systems.** “Do not break X” ⇒ X is read-only unless a surgical, re-verified fix is required.
9. **Translate intent into proof.** Every non-trivial claim ends in assets-in-repo, builds green, and checklist evidence — not vibes.

