## §B — Best possible designs + PNG/SVG assets (your paragraph B, enhanced)

> *You asked:* best possible designs; like PNG and SVG — not just icons but panels, illustrations and more; generate these or extract them from the web.

### B.1 Best possible designs — agent translation

**MUST**

- Treat every user-visible surface as a **designed product surface**, not “CSS that compiles.”
- **Reference before inventing.** Open top products in the category and craft libraries (for BNDZ: Uiverse and project visual rules). Study composition, materials, motion, empty states — then **adapt** into the project’s tokens/CSS.
- Hit a professional craft bar: clear hierarchy, depth, materials (glass/paper/metal/ink as fits), purposeful motion, one coherent composition per surface.
- Design **all states**: default, hover/press, focus, empty, loading, error, success.
- Ship **2–3 intentional motions** on visually led work (enter, hover/press, success/empty) — presence, not noise.
- Match the repo design system when it exists. For net-new UI, define CSS variables and a coherent direction — avoid generic AI clichés (purple SaaS cards, cream-serif posters, pill clusters, glow soup).

**MUST NOT**

- Ship UI that becomes “any SaaS dashboard” after removing the brand.
- Call a color/border/title tweak a “redesign.”
- Leave panels as raw text + default buttons when illustration or panel art would finish them.
- Paste raw third-party HTML/Tailwind/CDN widgets; adapt into local tokens/components.

### B.2 PNG and SVG — not only icons (panels, illustrations, and more)

**MUST prefer real assets** on surfaces that users stare at:

| Asset | Use for |
|-------|---------|
| **SVG** | Crisp chrome, illustrations, empty states, badges, panel ornaments, diagrams, decorative structure, scalable icons |
| **PNG** (WebP ok when appropriate) | Rich panels, hero/atmosphere art, textures, certificates, painted/soft illustration, product imagery |

**Explicitly in scope (not “icons only”):**

- Panel backgrounds and panel ornaments  
- Empty-state and onboarding illustrations  
- Certificates / plaques / portal art  
- Plugin and dialog decorative structure  
- Section illustrations and diagram SVGs  
- Toolbar/list icons *in addition to* the above — icons alone do **not** satisfy this paragraph  

**MUST NOT** rely on emoji, Unicode glyphs, or icon-row soup as the whole design.

### B.3 Generate **or** extract from the web

Agents **must obtain production assets** when craft needs them. Skipping both paths fails this paragraph.

**Path 1 — Generate**

1. Use available generators (e.g. Cursor image generation) for custom panel art, illustrations, certificates, icons, textures.
2. Prefer SVG for flat/vector; PNG/WebP for rich/soft imagery.
3. Optimize, name clearly (kebab-case), commit under the project asset folder.
4. **Wire into the real UI** so the asset is visible — unused files do not count.

**Path 2 — Extract / download from the web**

1. Download permissively licensed SVG/PNG packs, illustration kits, icon sets, GitHub `raw` assets from open repos.
2. Prefer MIT / Apache / CC0 / CC-BY (attribute when required). No proprietary scrapes.
3. Official brand assets only when allowed and appropriate.
4. Same: local copy, optimize, wire into UI.

**Always**

- Store under version control (`src/assets/`, `public/`, `Resources/`, …). No fragile CDN hotlinks for core UI.
- Light provenance (name + license + URL) for named packs; skip bureaucracy for tiny self-made glyphs.
- Size for real display (1x/2x); clean SVGs; no multi‑MB blobs on hot paths.

```text
❌ BAD: empty state = gray box + “No items”
✅ GOOD: custom SVG/PNG illustration + short copy + one action, on-brand materials, asset committed and rendered
```

