## §D — Verification system (your paragraph D, enhanced)

> *You asked:* a well thought-out system for verifying and checking code and design quality, checking builds for build errors, and proper debugging.

This is the **mandatory proof loop**. No proof → not done.

### D.1 System overview (well thought-out)

```text
Pre-flight → Implement (slice + cheap checks) → Design QA → Code QA → Build gate → Debug if needed → Honest status
```

Every implementation turn runs this loop. Agents do not stop at “it looks fine in my head.”

### D.2 Pre-flight

1. Restate the user goal (internally) + list **acceptance checks**.  
2. Mark **protect zones**.  
3. Note repo build/lint/test commands (project rules may name them).  
4. UI work: which **references + PNG/SVG assets** (§B).  
5. Non-trivial work: which **META stack** (§C.3–C.4).  

### D.3 During implementation

1. Track acceptance checks; mark as you go.  
2. After meaningful slices: cheapest check (types, unit test, lint on touched files, targeted build).  
3. Continuously judge UI against the craft bar — “it renders” is not design QA.  
4. If stuck → **D.6 debugging**, not random rewrites.  

### D.4 Design quality verification

Before claiming UI done:

- [ ] Intentional composition (not a dashboard dump unless it is one)  
- [ ] Compared to at least one strong visual reference  
- [ ] Real **PNG/SVG** craft where panels/illustrations/empty states need it — not icons alone  
- [ ] Theme/tokens honored  
- [ ] Empty / loading / error / success designed  
- [ ] Motion purposeful; no layout thrash / ~10fps interaction  
- [ ] Survives “remove the logo” brand test when branding matters  
- [ ] Assets committed **and** visible in built UI  

### D.5 Code quality verification

- [ ] Happy path end-to-end on the real surface  
- [ ] Failure paths useful (UI or logs); no silent swallow  
- [ ] No new lint/type errors in touched files  
- [ ] Protect zones re-verified if touched  
- [ ] Dead code/imports you introduced removed  
- [ ] FE/BE contracts match when both changed  
- [ ] New dependencies justified and resolve  

### D.6 Build gate — catch build errors

- Run required builds **before** telling the user it is ready.  
- **Build errors, type errors, restore failures = blockers.** Fix root cause → rebuild. Never “try anyway.”  
- For BNDZ product code/assets at minimum:

```bash
npm run build
dotnet build BNDZBackend/BNDZ.csproj -c Debug -p:EnableWindowsTargeting=true
```

- Run project lint/tests when they exist and apply.  
- Skip builds only for pure docs/rules/questions with **zero** product code or asset changes.  
- When claiming done, know what you ran and the outcome.  

### D.7 Proper debugging

1. **Reproduce** (or confirm via build/log/test evidence).  
2. **Locate** the owning system; read surrounding code first.  
3. **Hypothesize narrowly**; change one cause at a time when possible.  
4. **Fix the cause**; guards only for real invariants.  
5. **Re-verify** the bug + nearby protect behaviors.  
6. Use the right tools: logs/debugger, bisect on regressions, WebView/browser inspector, native traces.  
7. Never “fix” by disabling features or deleting libraries unless the user ordered removal.  
8. If evidence can’t be gathered (e.g. needs Windows host), status = **Blocked** + what is missing — never fake a pass.  

### D.8 Honest status

- **Done** = acceptance checks + design/code QA + builds green + no known broken in-scope paths.  
- **Blocked** = evidence of the blocker.  
- No filler plans; no unsigned checklist pretend-signed.  

```text
❌ BAD: “should work, refresh” after CSS with no build; “debug” by rewriting at random
✅ GOOD: assets in repo → design QA → code QA → builds green → debug with repro/logs → status matches reality
```

